kernel-form \ Two variables whose names differ only in case, and nothing else: here a
\ spelling check that ignored case would not stop the run (as declaring
\ both id and Id does in 14-case.lf); it would silently make X mean x.
\ The round trip cannot see that, since the printer and the words would
\ agree; the comparison with Lean's #print does (ADR 0017 section 13).
\ Lean: def caseVar {X : Type} (x : X) : X := x
def caseVar
  0 Type implicit: X
  X explicit: x
  X
:=
  x
end caseVar
